-- title:
--   Correspondence 7.13 — bottlenecks correspond to $r$-local bottlenecks
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a connected graph whose binary cycle space is generated by cycles of length at most $r$, and let $k\in\mathbb N$. The map
--   $$\beta\longmapsto\beta_r=\{s_r:s\in\beta\}$$
--   is a bijection from the $k$-bottlenecks in $G$ onto the $r$-local $k$-bottlenecks in $G$: it maps $k$-bottlenecks to $r$-local $k$-bottlenecks, it is injective on them, and every $r$-local $k$-bottleneck is of this form.
--
--   Applied in the $r$-local covering, this transfers statements about bottlenecks to $r$-local bottlenecks.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - reading: the binary cycle space of $G$ is generated by cycles of length $\le r$ → every cycle's edge set is a finite symmetric difference of edge sets of cycles of length $\le r$ (`CycleSpaceGenByShort`); reason: the finite cycle space; the proofs (Lemma 4.3, Correspondence 4.4) argue with finite $\mathbb Z/2$ sums
--   - encoding: orders $|X|$ of separators → `Set.encard` in $\mathbb N_\infty$; reason: separators of the infinite cover can be infinite (p.29); no finite instance changes
-- source:
--   Jacobs, Knappe, Kurkofka, Canonical Graph Decompositions via Local Separations, preprint (STOC 2027 submission, arXiv:2501.16170; sha256 9a11d48d…), Correspondence 7.13, p.46

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_LocalSepDecomp_Cutouts

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace LocalSepDecomp

open SimpleGraph

universe u

/-- **Correspondence 7.13** (Local bottlenecks). R. W. Jacobs, P. Knappe, J. Kurkofka, *Canonical Graph Decompositions via Local Separations*,
preprint (STOC 2027 submission, arXiv:2501.16170; sha256 9a11d48d…), Correspondence 7.13, p.46.
Assume that the binary cycle space of `G` is generated by cycles of length `≤ r` and that `G` is
connected. The map `β ↦ β_r = {s_r : s ∈ β}` is a bijection between the `k`-bottlenecks in `G`
and the `r`-local `k`-bottlenecks in `G`. -/
theorem correspondence_7_13 {V : Type u} (G : SimpleGraph V) (r : ℕ)
    (hcyc : CycleSpaceGenByShort G r) (hG : G.Connected) (k : ℕ) :
    (∀ β, IsBottleneck G k β → IsLocalBottleneck G r k (bottleneckToLocal G β)) ∧
      Set.InjOn (bottleneckToLocal G) {β | IsBottleneck G k β} ∧
      ∀ β' : Set (ULSep V), IsLocalBottleneck G r k β' →
        ∃ β, IsBottleneck G k β ∧ bottleneckToLocal G β = β' := by sorry

end LocalSepDecomp
